  {
   "evidence_id": "pr:jrnl-org/jrnl#2120:comment:0",
   "payload": {
    "author": "MohammedAlkindi",
    "author_is_bot": false,
    "body": "Checked this out on Windows 11 / Python 3.14.7 and it does what the description says.\n\nBefore, on `main`:\n\n```\npython -m jrnl: error: argument --format: invalid choice: 'whatformats'\n(choose from 'boxed', 'calendar', 'dates', 'fancy', 'heatmap', 'json', 'markdown',\n 'md', 'pretty', 'short', 'tags', 'text', 'txt', 'xml', 'yaml')\n```\n\nOn this branch:\n\n```\npython -m jrnl: error: argument --format: not allowed with argument --import\n```\n\n`tests/unit/test_parse_args.py` gives 55 passed, and the full suite on this branch is 696 passed, 44 skipped.\n\nOne thing I could not check: whether `--format` still behaves for a normal export. My run hit first-run journal setup rather than the export path, so that is my environment and not evidence either way about this change.\n\nRan the commands above myself; the write-up was drafted with AI assistance.\n"
   },
