    "body": "Reproduced and confirmed on Windows 11 / Python 3.14.7. Probe: https://gist.github.com/MohammedAlkindi/9e2161d587c805fea4bc4f41b1c38feb\n\nOn `main` at `90de494`, then on this branch at `83a1247`:\n\n```\ninput                       main            this branch\n'### heading'               ['###']         []\n'@#@'                       ['@#']          []\n'####'                      ['####']        []\n'## heading with #realtag'  ['##','#realtag'] ['#realtag']\n'#realtag and @person'      unchanged       unchanged\n```\n\nFull suite on this branch is 694 passed, 44 skipped, and `tests/unit/test_entry.py` is 3 passed.\n\nOne correction to the description rather than the code: `@@` is listed as an affected case, but it already returns `[]` on `main`. The trailing class is `[-+*#/\\w]`, which contains `#` but not `@`, so `@@` never matched the pattern in the first place. The other three cases do reproduce exactly as described.\n"
   },
